If a patient receives a long-term-opioid-therapy then every clinician should regularly reassess the patient.
If a patient receives a long-term-opioid-therapy then every clinician should consider a suggested-long-term-opioid-reassessment-schedule for the patient.
If a clinician uses a suggested-long-term-opioid-reassessment-schedule for a patient then the clinician reassesses the patient at an interval of at most 3 months.
If a clinician sees a new-patient and the new-patient receives a long-term-opioid-therapy then the clinician should regularly reassess the new-patient.
